/-!
# An active chief section generated by the original M22 moved seed

Inside the literal image J of RH in N(U)/U, let W=[B/U,R] and let E be its
normal closure in J. The original pair places E in O₂(J). The seed survives
E/Φ(E), since otherwise the characteristic Frattini subgroup would contain
all of its generating conjugates.

The native multiplicity action supplies an actual element of O²(I) fixing
no nonidentity element of P/U. It therefore moves E; Burnside's Frattini
kernel theorem detects this two-perfect action on E/Φ(E). An actual chief
interval above Φ(E), inside E, is then selected with nontrivial action of
the same original O²(I), retaining its literal quotient-map formula.

These chief factors are subquotients of the particular seed-generated
Frattini module. Identifying their natural R-type and their precise
V-displacement is the subsequent representation-theoretic source step.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith 8.2.8(5) and 8.2.9, printed pp.718--721,
refs/quasithin.pdf.
-/

public noncomputable section
open Subgroup Representation Representation.BinaryOffender Theory.GroupTheory
